class_name UiIcons
extends RefCounted
## THE UI ICON BANK — thirty-four marks, drawn on a 16x16 grid, in code.
##
## Pete, 13 Sep 2026: *"I see even Retro Bowl and icons and stars in places...
## I'd like to see all the UI more 8-bit themed and maybe something akin to menu
## flair."*
##
## WHY THESE ARE NOT PNGs, and it is not laziness. This codebase already draws
## its heraldry as pixel grids in `IconBank` and builds its typefaces the same
## way out of `glyphs.py`, so a grid here is the existing pattern rather than a
## new one — and it buys four things an imported file never will:
##
##   * **no licence.** Nothing to credit, nothing to keep a copy of, nothing
##     that can turn out to be CC-BY-SA the week before launch.
##   * **no import step.** No `.import` file, no reimport, no texture that
##     silently comes back filtered and soft.
##   * **perfect grid alignment.** These are 16 pixels, drawn at whole-pixel
##     positions, at integer scales. An imported 96x96 icon scaled to 16 is mush
##     and scaled to 24 is mush at a different size.
##   * **it recolors for free.** Every mark takes a `Color`, so the mood swap
##     carries the icons with it and nobody has to author five tinted copies.
##
## THE VOCABULARY IS BORROWED, and that is the useful half of the work somebody
## already did. ACRTW ships 33 UI icons and 19 HUD ones, all smooth vector
## silhouettes at 96x96 — the wrong style entirely, and the right LIST. The
## buhurt-specific half of it in particular (anvil, round shield, shoulder
## armor, wolf, fist) is a vocabulary written down by somebody who fights.
## These are those ideas redrawn on a grid this game can use.
##
## WHAT MAKES A 16x16 ICON READ, learned by drawing six that did not: a hard
## silhouette and one pixel of internal negative space. Two-pixel strokes fill
## the shape in and every icon comes out a blob — the first shield read as a
## bucket, the first helm as a box, the first cuirass as a horseshoe.

## `#` is ink, `.` is nothing. Sixteen rows of sixteen, every one — asserted in
## `test_icons.gd`, because a grid that is fifteen wide draws a mark one pixel
## narrow and nobody notices until it is beside another one.
